gured for SuccessFactors Learning Integration URI and SuccessFactors Learning Integration API URI in Company Settings in SuccessFactors platform (BizX) Provisioning # The value was last queried from SuccessFactors platform (BizX) Provisioning on [] successFactorsLearningURL=https://dfohrsandbox-stage.lms.hr.cloud.sap"}},{"IsSelected":true,"Selector":"<ctrl name=\"# Learning Integration enabled - set to true to enable integrati*\" role=\"cell\"/>","ValidAttributes":{"name":"# Learning Integration enabled - set to true to enable integrati*","role":"cell","aastate":"opaque"}},{"IsSelected":true,"Selector":"<ctrl name=\"Konfigurasjon\" role=\"editable text\"/>","ValidAttributes":{"name":"Konfigurasjon","role":"editable text","aastate":"har fokus, fokuserbar, editable, multiline, opaque, selectable text","text":"# Learning Integration enabled - set to true to enable integration between SF\n# learning and the SF main application.\n# Whenever you change the successFactorsLearningEnabled configuration,\n# a background job is triggered to update the cards on the latest home page.\n# This job may run with a delay and the cards are updated after the job is completed.\nsuccessFactorsLearningEnabled=true\n\n# The baseURL is used to generate client-friendly URLs to BizX services (e.g.\n# deeplinks, serverPing, oAuth token server, etc.). This URL must be client-\n# friendly, meaning it needs to be resolvable from the browser.\n# Whenever you change the baseURL configuration,\n# a background job is triggered to update the cards on the latest home page.\n# This job may run with a delay and the cards are updated after the job is completed.\nbaseURL=https://hcm-eu20-preview.hr.cloud.sap\n\n# SuccessFactors Company ID for the current tenant. This will use the LMS\n# tenant ID by default, so it is recommended to keep the SF company ID and\n# LMS tenant ID in sync in production.\n# Whenever you change the successFactorsCompanyID configuration,\n# a background job is triggered to update the cards on the latest home page.\n# This job may run with a delay and the cards are updated after the job is completed.\nsuccessFactorsCompanyID=dfohrsandbox\n\n# successFactorsDeepLinkPath is used to generate deep links to the system when\n# running in integration mode. This will be appended to the baseURL, and does\n# not need a trailing slash. The deep link URL will be generated according to\n# the following pattern:\n# http://${baseURL}/${successFactorsDeepLinkPath}?destUrl=<URL of specific learning in Plateau>\nsuccessFactorsDeepLinkPath=/sf/learning\n\n# successFactorsServerPingPath is used to ping the SF server to keep the\n# Learning session alive. This will be appended to the baseURL, and does not\n# need a trailing slash. The ping URL will be generated according to the\n# following pattern:\n# https://${baseURL}/${successFactorsServerPingPath}\nsuccessFactorsServerPingPath=/sf/ping\n\n# successFactorsHomePath is deeplink to SF Home.\n# This will be appended to the baseURL, and does not need a trailing slash.\n# The admin tools URL will be generated according to the\n# following pattern:\n# https://${baseURL}/${successFactorsHomePath}\nsuccessFactorsHomePath=/sf/home\n\n# successFactorsAdminToolsPath is deeplink to SF Admin Tools.\n# This will be appended to the baseURL, and does not need a trailing slash.\n# The admin tools URL will be generated according to the\n# following pattern:\n# https://${baseURL}/${successFactorsAdminToolsPath}\nsuccessFactorsAdminToolsPath=/sf/admin\n\n# The SF logout path\n# This will be appended to the baseURL, and does not need a trailing slash.\n# The admin tools URL will be generated according to the\n# following pattern:  https://${baseURL}/${successFactorsLogoutPath}\nsuccessFactorsLogoutPath=/sf/logout\n\n# showNewsInIntegratedMode controls whether the news page popup on the learning home page.\nshowNewsInIntegratedMode=true\n\n# Enable LMS Ultra UI - set to true to support SF Ultra UI\n#This should be false if branding is being applied.\nultraUIEnabled=false\nremoveActivitiesAddedviaCDPfromLMS=false\n\n# User/Supervisor cannot remove the activities from the user's assignment,\n# if the course was added via development Goals.\npreventDeletionOfActivitiesAddedViaCDPFromLMS=false\n\n# The Due Date of the Development Goal in CDP will be set as the Required Date for the Item when added from CDP.\n# The date would Not be updated in LMS even if there are any changes made to the due date of the development goal in CDP.\nsetCDPGoalDueDateAsRequiredDate=false\n\n# ==================================================\n#  SAML Single Sign On\n# ==================================================\n\n# The Default IDP metadataProvider to use. Must be set to one of the IDP\n# metadataProviders configured below.\ndefaultIDP=IDP1\nmetadataProviders.IDP1.type=SuccessFactorsHTTPMetadataProvider\nmetadataProviders.IDP1.value=https://hcm-eu20-preview.hr.cloud.sap/idp/samlmetadata?company=dfohrsandbox\n\n# Example of a ClassPathResourceMetadataProvider usage.\n# metadataProviders[IDP2].type=ClassPathResourceMetadataProvider\n# metadataProviders[IDP2].value=myCustomerSamlIDP.xml\n\n# Client browsers are redirected to the samlLoginURL when a login is required.\nsamlLoginURL=/saml/login\n\n# Client browsers are redirected to the samlSSOProcessingURL during SSO with\n# SAML.\nsamlSSOProcessingURL=/saml/SSO\n\n# The single sign out service URL of the the Learning Server. This endpoint\n# processes the SAML single logout request.\nsingleLogoutServiceURL=/saml/SingleLogout\n\n# The SAML metadata provider URL.\nsamlMetadataURL=/saml/metadata\n\n# The SAML logout processing URL for the samlLogoutFilter.\nsamlLogoutProcessingURL=/saml/logout\n\n# Target URL after successfully logged out\nsamlLogoutSuccessURL=/saml/logout.jsp\n\n# Establish a new session for each LMS direct link coming from BizX. This includes accesssing LMS from BizX, various CDP areas and etc\nnewSessionForEachDeeplinkFromBizX=true\n\n# When set to true, it will wrap incoming native deep link requests with the BizX URL. Then it will redirect the client to the wrapped deeplink.\nwrapNativeDeeplinksWithBizXURL=false\n\n# ==================================================\n# Jam (formerly called CubeTree) Integration\n# ==================================================\n\n# The successFactorsCubeTreeBaseURL is used by the Learning server to make\n# server-to-server calls to Jam.  The default value must be updated to a valid\n# value for the Jam integration to be available.\nsuccessFactorsCubeTreeBaseURL=https://cubetree-server\n\n# Forces JAM notifications to be sent out from Jam only.\n# If set to false, the system will send JAM notifications from the LMS as well, possibly resulting in duplicate emails.\nsuppressJamNotificationsFromLMS=true\n\n# Enables Workzone integration\nworkzoneEnabled=false\n\n# The client key for the OAuth client added in Workzone. This is required if Workzone is enabled.\nclientKey=\n\n# The IDP ID used when registering the SAML Trusted IDP in Workzone. This is required if Workzone is enabled.\nidpId=\n\n# The private key of the Base64 encoded key pair used when registering the SAML Trusted IDP in Workzone. This is required if Workzone is enabled.\nworkzonePrivateKey=\n\n# If this value is true then users will not see the Community tab. Instead a Launch button appears that opens the item's associated Jam/WZ community group in a new window.\n# If this value is false then users will see the Community tab. Selecting the item's associated Jam/WZ community group will open the selection in an iFrame.\nopenJamInNewBrowserWindow=false\n\n# ==================================================\n# Session Management Service Integration\n# ==================================================\n\n# With this setting disabled, Session Management service ping is not used for keep alive of BizX while user is taking online content\n# In that case, only the browser based ping to BizX is used.\nsessionMgmtNotifyModuleActivity=false\n\n# ==================================================\n# External User Integration\n# ==================================================\n\n# Enables the creation of a BizX user when a user creates an account via a site that does not require approval for registration.\n# A value of true is only supported if successFactorsLearningEnabled=true. Default: false\ncreateIntegratedExternalUser=false\n\n#comma separated contact email ids of Sensitive Private Data Point of Contact\nsensitivePrivateDataContactEmailList=\n\n# This is the value of the URL configured for SuccessFactors Learning Integration URI and SuccessFactors Learning Integration API URI in Company Settings in SuccessFactors platform (BizX) Provisioning\n# The value was last queried from SuccessFactors platform (BizX) Provisioning on []\nsuccessFactorsLearningURL=https://dfohrsandbox-stage.lms.hr.cloud.sap"}}]}}